From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:55:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 060/154] fix: give every chrome surface a delegate so its
 unhandled keys come back
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WebContentsImpl::HandleKeyboardEvent short-circuits on `delegate_ && ...`, so a
WebContents with no delegate drops every key the renderer declined - the
renderer's unhandled ack never becomes a redispatch and the chord dies in
silence. Every surface built through CreateChromeContents was delegate-less;
Cmd+S dying on the foyer is what surfaced it.

ChromeSurfaceKeyForwarder is the forwarding PeekWidget already did by hand,
now the default for every such surface. A surface that wants its own delegate
still calls SetDelegate after CreateChromeContents.

The rest is the instrument that found it, kept because it answers "where did
the chord die" in one line: a Cmd+S dead-chord probe naming the responder's
actual page rather than its responder class (every WebContents-backed surface
answers to the same class), and one VLOG on each of the three places a key can
stop - the widget's ack, the WebContents' delegate hop, and the window's
redispatch.

CreateForTesting/ResetForTesting bind the leaked singleton to a profile
synchronously so the delegate wiring is unit-testable at all.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc        | 13 +++++++++++++
 content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc   |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
index 01d72aba68bff..82924fdcb38d0 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
@@ -2665,6 +2665,19 @@ void RenderWidgetHostImpl::OnKeyboardEventAck(
   bool processed =
       (blink::mojom::InputEventResultState::kConsumed == ack_result);
 
+  // A command chord the renderer declines has to come back up here
+  // to be redispatched. Say whether it did, and if not what stopped it.
+  if (event.event.GetType() == blink::WebInputEvent::Type::kRawKeyDown &&
+      (event.event.GetModifiers() & blink::WebInputEvent::kMetaKey)) {
+    const char* stop = !delegate_          ? "no-delegate"
+                       : processed         ? "renderer-consumed"
+                       : IsHidden()        ? "hidden"
+                       : event.event.skip_if_unhandled ? "skip-if-unhandled"
+                                                       : "forwarded";
+    VLOG(1) << "Atrium: keyack rwh=" << GetRoutingID()
+            << " key=" << event.event.windows_key_code << " stop=" << stop;
+  }
+
   // We only send unprocessed key event upwards if we are not hidden,
   // because the user has moved away from us and no longer expect any effect
   // of this key event.
diff --git a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
index 7edad76e875c0..e7653cbcd5081 100644
--- a/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/web_contents/web_contents_impl.cc
@@ -4680,6 +4680,14 @@ bool WebContentsImpl::HandleKeyboardEvent(
       browser_plugin_embedder_->HandleKeyboardEvent(event)) {
     return true;
   }
+  // A surface with no delegate ends the unhandled-key trip here,
+  // and does it silently. Name the surface and say which way it went.
+  if (event.GetType() == blink::WebInputEvent::Type::kRawKeyDown &&
+      (event.GetModifiers() & blink::WebInputEvent::kMetaKey)) {
+    VLOG(1) << "Atrium: wc handlekey url=" << GetLastCommittedURL().spec()
+            << " key=" << event.windows_key_code
+            << " stop=" << (delegate_ ? "to-delegate" : "no-delegate");
+  }
   return delegate_ && delegate_->HandleKeyboardEvent(this, event);
 }
 
